          %title Basic notions of Topos theory
          %h2#BasicNotionsOfToposTheory Basic notions of Topos theory
          %p
            We have explained in Remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresaheavesAsGeneralizedSpaces"}
            how
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            may be thought of as
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
                probe-able by the objects of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            (Prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaLemma"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            (Prop.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#YonedaEmbedding"}
            %em locality
            or
            %em gluing condition
            (Remark
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheafConditionAsLocality"}
            below), to be called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            condition (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SheafConditionAsLocality"}
            below).
          %p
            More in detail, we had seen that any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            of the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            (Prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeCocompletion"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X} \in [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
            as being glued or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generated
            form the “ordinary spaces”
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{C}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} relations
            among these generators, such as the locality relation embodied by the
            = succeed "-condition." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
          %p
            It turns out that these relations are reflected by special properties of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointFunctorsInTermsOfNaturalBijectionOfHomSets"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
            to ordinary
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces"} spaces
          %p
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+spaces"} generalized spaces
              via
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generators and relations
