          #CanonicalCoverageOnTopologicalSpaces.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (canonical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
                on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              of (small)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
              (Example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesOfConcreteCategories"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Coverage"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverings"} coverings
              are the usal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
              of topological spaces.
            %p
              The condition
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ConditionOnCoverage"} (1)
              on a coverage is met, since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimages"} preimages
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              under a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+function"} continuous function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              are again
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
              = succeed "-condition" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ConditionOnCoverage"} (1)
              is immediage.
            %p
              Similarly, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in Top
              a fixed topological space, there is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Op(X)
              whose underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+opens"} category of opens
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thin+category"} thin category
              (Example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PartiallyOrderedSetsAsSmallCategories"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and subset inclusions, and whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverings"} coverings
              are again the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
          #DifferentiablyGoodOpenCoversOfSmoothManifolds.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (differentiably
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+covers"} good open covers
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              (Example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExamplesOfConcreteCategories"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              (Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Coverage"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SmthMfd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in SmthMfd
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverings"} coverings
              are collections of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^D
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              is the inclusion of an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
            %p
              Hence these are the usual
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+covers"} open covers
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
              to a Cartesian space (hence to a smooth
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+ball"} open ball
            %p
              One may further constrain this and ask that also all the non-empty finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersections"} intersections
              of these open balls are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
              to open balls. These are the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  differentiably
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+covers"} good open covers
            %p
              To see that these coverings satisfy the condition
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ConditionOnCoverage"} (1)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              along any continuous function is again an open cover, just not necessarily by patches diffeomorphic to open balls. But every open cover may be
              %em refined
              by one that is (see at
              = succeed ")," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ConditionOnCoverage"} (1)
          %p
            Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DifferentiablyGoodOpenCoversOfSmoothManifolds"}
            is further developed in the chapters
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            and
            = succeed "." do
